    compiler_interpreter_integration_real_gaps_found_2026-09-06, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: per-gap matrix on a scratch build of HEAD (build/p3cache/fresh-seed/simple-head.exe vs simple-patched.exe). Gap 1 (ambiguous method call): CLOSED at tip - hard error (impl_duplicate_check.rs, PR #7597). Gap 2 (annotated type vs literal): CLOSED at tip - hard error (same PR). Gap 3 (div-zero span): was LIVE (exit 1 with file:3:1 but no literal line 3) - FIXED: ops.rs division_by_zero_error now pub(super) and span-aware + units.rs 5 inline raises unified; message now division by zero (at line 3, column 1). Gap 4 (export visibility): was LIVE (same-dir use mod.{_secret_add} exit 0) - FIXED: module_loader.rs same-dir sibling exemption now per-name and no longer covers _-prefixed top-level fns (dir exemption moved out of fn_visibility_outcome into the two call-rule helpers with identical call behavior; touching the call rule was too risky - 34k _ fns); mirrored in pure-Simple module_import_resolution.spl (private_fn_import_denied). Gap 5 (circular import): was LIVE (mutual val import exit 0) - FIXED: circular arm now hard-errors when a braced use names a top-level VALUE binding the in-flight module cannot provide yet; cyclic FUNCTION imports keep the partial path (stdlib deliberately uses cyclic fn imports - first iteration broke it, caught by the harness, refined); CIRCULAR_IMPORT_MARKER propagation in evaluation_helpers.rs/export_handler.rs so the error is not degraded to an empty dict. Regression specs (test/01_unit/compiler/95.interp/interpreter/): division_by_zero_span_diagnostic 0/2 to 2/2, underscore_private_fn_import_visibility 1/2 to 2/2, circular_value_import_detection 2/3 to 3/3 (pins fn-cycle tolerance + acyclic control) - all RED on unpatched, GREEN on patched. Fallout: private_fn_import_visibility_enforcement 5/5, strict_interp 10/10, unit_div_remainder_native 8/8, impl-duplicate/let-literal specs pass; full stdlib loads through the patched loader with no false positives. Residuals: gap 3 JIT lane still hardware-traps x/0 (deliberate sdiv; needs a runtime raise hook - the tracked scenario runs on the interpreter lane); gap 4 leaves same-dir calls and glob/non-group imports of _ names unchecked; gap 5 leaves non-group/glob/type cycles tolerated by design. Re-verification recipe (exact cargo command, repro script, expected outputs): build/p3cache/compint/REVERIFICATION.md. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/95.interp/interpreter/division_by_zero_span_diagnostic_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/95.interp/interpreter/circular_value_import_detection_spec.spl"

